    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Tesla returns twelve weeks after the increase to sertraline 150 mg. At the nurse telephone check two weeks after the increase he reported mild sweating and no other side effects. He now has mild delayed ejaculation, which he finds acceptable, and has missed no doses. The Y-BOCS his therapist was to rate at about week eighteen was not done: that session was spent on an exposure at his laboratory and no rating was rescheduled. He has had eighteen ERP sessions and will finish the course next month. His rituals take about 45 minutes a day; he still counts steps on some walks but can stop. He eats three meals a day without calculating, sleeps about six hours, and has stopped working after midnight. He has had no suicidal thoughts. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Missed rating</td><td>Therapist&apos;s Y-BOCS at about week eighteen not done</td></tr><tr><td>Sertraline</td><td>Mild sweating and delayed ejaculation; no missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Rituals</td><td>About 45 minutes a day</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition and sleep</td><td>Three meals a day; about six hours of sleep</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>Y-BOCS</td><td>13, down from 28</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

