    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Obsessive-compulsive disorder, responding (F42.2)</content>. Y-BOCS 13, down 54 percent from 28: a clear response after twelve weeks at 150 mg with ERP. PHQ-9 3 and GAD-7 5. Delayed ejaculation is mild and acceptable to him. Suicide risk remains low. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 150 mg for at least one to two years before any slow taper.</item><item>Finish the ERP course, then monthly booster sessions; relapse-prevention plan with his therapist.</item><item>Collaborative safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Underweight, resolved (R63.6)</content>. 66.9 kg, BMI 18.9; albumin 4.2 g/dL and vitamin B12 412 pg/mL. [S]<list><item>Keep three meals a day; weight at each visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Insufficient sleep, resolved (Z72.820)</content>. About six hours a night with no work after midnight. [S]<list><item>Keep the fixed sleep window.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Y-BOCS severity score (recorded in the note; no LOINC code found)</td><td>At baseline and about every 4 to 6 weeks during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>13, down 54 percent from 28: response</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Interim Y-BOCS between the twelve-week review and today</td><td>At baseline and about every 4 to 6 weeks during acute treatment</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not done, a deviation from the protocol: the therapist&apos;s Y-BOCS planned at about week eighteen was not done because that session was used for an exposure and no rating was rescheduled, leaving twelve weeks without a severity score during the titration. No harm resulted judging by today&apos;s score and review: he responded and had no suicidal thoughts. Corrective action: the therapist now enters a Y-BOCS in the shared record every sixth session, and the clinic registry flags a missing score</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9 and GAD-7 for secondary depression and anxiety</td><td>At baseline and periodically while depressive or anxiety symptoms are present</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 3 (item 9 scored 0); GAD-7 5</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9 when given)</td><td>Every visit during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, or behavior since the last visit; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0. Protective factors stronger than at intake. Safety plan reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Sertraline adherence and adverse effects (nausea, diarrhea, sleep, activation, sexual effects)</td><td>Every visit and two weeks after each dose increase</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Nurse call two weeks after the increase: mild sweating only. Today mild delayed ejaculation, acceptable to him; no missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exposure and response prevention attendance and homework</td><td>Every visit during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Eighteen sessions; course ends next month; booster sessions planned</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI</td><td>Every visit while underweight</td><td>Completed today</td><td>66.9 kg, BMI 18.9, up 3.1 kg since intake</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Albumin and vitamin B12 after dietary change</td><td>Once, after about six months of better intake</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Albumin 4.2 g/dL; vitamin B12 412 pg/mL</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sleep diary</td><td>Every visit during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About six hours a night</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antipsychotic augmentation monitoring (weight, glucose, lipids, movement)</td><td>Only if an antipsychotic is added</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No augmentation; responding to sertraline and ERP</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Y-BOCS down by at least 35 percent (treatment response) by twenty-four weeks. Outcome by 1902-06-30: Y-BOCS 13 at twenty-four weeks, down 54 percent from 28 [S]</item><item>Rituals under one hour a day, with meals eaten without calculating. Outcome by 1902-06-30: Rituals about 45 minutes a day; most meals eaten without calculation [S]</item><item>BMI at least 18.5 with three meals a day. Outcome by 1902-06-30: Weight 66.9 kg, BMI 18.9 [S]</item><item>Hands healed, with washing under 15 times a day. Outcome by 1902-04-07: Skin healed; washing about 12 times a day by twelve weeks [S]</item><item>At least six hours of sleep most nights. Outcome by 1902-06-30: About six hours most nights [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Patients With Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (2007); Guideline Watch: Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Patients With Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (2013); Obsessive-compulsive disorder and body dysmorphic disorder: treatment (CG31) (2005); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Preventive visit in October; OCD review in about three months. Next scheduled visit 1902-10-13: periodic adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

